#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054365 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93bc0caa-2352-5d02-9ccf-7267dff4be2c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "a8c9f90f-3c97-5a01-99b5-9a9f8b3eef66" :question/math-academy-id "e-12677" :question/problem "Consider the following statement:\n\n$14$ is divisible by $4$ **or** $\\sqrt{3}$ is a rational number.\n\nWrite this statement in symbolic form using the following notations:\n\n- ![](images/43/437d6f4601c7ccb76c02bdffecd0079dd3beb5bb4faf41c2d3074617b8a3b069.png)\n\n- ![](images/10/10bd9b53b9b98734e5e1052927d77f02b46556e61e51663de34e66b303edfc9e.png)" :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{14 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is divisible by }\\vphantom{p} 4 }_S \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{\\sqrt{3} \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a rational number} }_T,\n$$\n\nthat is, $S \\lor T.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054366 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "e5a60113-14a0-5468-93b1-7f0eaa6e9a90" :question/math-academy-id "e-12678" :question/problem "$7$ is odd **or** a multiple of $3$, **and** $3$ is less than $7$.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- ![](images/63/6378f3d805dd0595262cbd3a955fa0b2b74f72dcef9e3384eaced510d4bc58fd.png)\n\n- ![](images/9e/9eebe764937f6efdf47efc63912838592ed023d0b42b670e0f83b5d9d837e41b.png)\n\n- ![](images/17/17cb303f80bb1b44c30b4c64e1101523b555cc34158f160dc68fd5f81826070e.png)" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $7$ is odd or a multiple of $3.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd }}_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a multiple of }3}_Q,\n$$\n\nthat is, $P \\lor Q.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $3$ is less than $7$. This corresponds to $R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd} \\textbf{ or } \\vphantom{p} \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ a multiple of } 3}_{P \\, \\lor \\,Q}, \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{3 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is less than } 7 }_R\n$$\n\nthat is, $(P \\lor Q) \\land R.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054368 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49ab93ca-16ca-5e57-835f-036b59f25d63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Compound Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "6497cb54-2453-5dd7-8b97-09e06280d774" :question/math-academy-id "e-12693" :question/problem "Consider the following compound statement:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{5 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is prime} }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{\\dfrac13 \\in \\mathbb{Z}}_B\n$$\n\nFind the truth values of the statements $A$ and $B,$ and the compound statement $A\\lor B.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{5\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{\\frac{1}{3}\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054389 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "9209c4e5-30e0-5933-9c41-32750b5301ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-12895" :question/problem "Consider the following compound statement:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\mathbb{Z}\\cup \\mathbb{R}=\\mathbb{Z} }_P \n\\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{\\overbrace{7 \\,|\\, 21}^Q \n\\quad \\overbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{or}}^{\\lor} \\quad \n\\overbrace{7 \\,|\\, 29}^R }_{Q \\, \\lor \\, R}\n$$\n\nFind the truth values of the statements $P,$ $Q$ and $R,$ and the compound statements $Q\\lor R$ and $P\\land (Q\\lor R).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is false, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q \\lor R$ is true, but the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{false}∧\\overset{\\text{true}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{true}∨\\text{false})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93bc0caa-2352-5d02-9ccf-7267dff4be2c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58f0507d-20d4-5775-b373-d900d8b96779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∧(X∨Y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389665} {:answer/id #uuid "74edb7a8-7861-5d22-ad52-5bf2049659b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y∧Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389666} {:answer/id #uuid "79bde983-110b-51ba-9196-948da1351529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∨Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389667} {:answer/id #uuid "98ad621e-6a51-525b-87d3-68cb43e74fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∧Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389668} {:answer/id #uuid "9a7c8e26-e02a-5580-a252-6eeef8520438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∨(X∧Y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98ad621e-6a51-525b-87d3-68cb43e74fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∧Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389668} :answer-field/id #uuid "40a5c6cf-be89-504a-bea5-37363120d54a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c84caa5-0818-5b64-a106-3aa76c7b323f" :question/math-academy-id "q-170738" :question/problem "Express the statement \"$4$ is even and positive\" in symbolic form, where $X=$ \"$4$ is even\" and $Y=$ \"$4$ is positive.\"" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nNote that the given sentence is a shortened version of the following full sentence:\n\n$4$ is even and $4$ is positive.\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{4\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{X}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{4\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{Y},\n$$\n\nthat is, $X∧Y.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379015 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49ab93ca-16ca-5e57-835f-036b59f25d63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Compound Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df22f795-a009-5641-a379-443361928638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379017} {:answer/id #uuid "de633a70-3263-5034-98fb-d53bce172bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de633a70-3263-5034-98fb-d53bce172bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379018} :answer-field/id #uuid "d51318db-0570-5f7c-be3d-fcaf41b4d016" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23d7849b-e56c-547e-bb92-1d1d1d8df933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379020} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb0cbad-92da-5755-8a8a-ee3831707436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23d7849b-e56c-547e-bb92-1d1d1d8df933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379020} :answer-field/id #uuid "e423f89e-f2a2-5170-a1c1-7dc0a236ee95" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379019} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b435872b-9826-56f1-933c-ff72d47f24d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379023} {:answer/id #uuid "4f4e19c2-8a61-5cca-a6c0-905cfac51eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b435872b-9826-56f1-933c-ff72d47f24d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379023} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c5f53eb-60e0-5636-a955-f574b8536172" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc4b578b-6250-5651-a423-a5ab765ad427" :question/math-academy-id "q-175912" :question/problem "$$\n{{3\\,|\\,9}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3\\,|\\,16}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∧B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{3\\,|\\,9}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3\\,|\\,16}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∧\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389724 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49ab93ca-16ca-5e57-835f-036b59f25d63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Compound Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29714588-6335-5a3d-9e8e-6b9fe2ff989d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389726} {:answer/id #uuid "b6fac748-5f68-5d84-84b4-0c2626ded647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6fac748-5f68-5d84-84b4-0c2626ded647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389727} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae63eeb-0ec3-5e40-b42d-72190c300318" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c02c34d4-7b0c-5b65-9668-0c6a9af1fbff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389729} {:answer/id #uuid "6adc1873-94c6-563f-9c49-fd5fb9a16778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6adc1873-94c6-563f-9c49-fd5fb9a16778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389730} :answer-field/id #uuid "574a91d1-41fa-5456-a8c8-197945bd4223" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389728} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5633f3b-27c0-5c52-8d2f-ac92c09e1805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389732} {:answer/id #uuid "610c67e2-723f-5d90-b263-aa6df2457a00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "610c67e2-723f-5d90-b263-aa6df2457a00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389733} :answer-field/id #uuid "0617aa93-4a98-5969-9378-7be2f4f05f2a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8dac36ef-0828-520a-adc1-0e3c49c1f35c" :question/math-academy-id "q-175913" :question/problem "$$\n{{\\sqrt{5}\\in R}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{10\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∧B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\sqrt{5}\\in R}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{10\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∧\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49ab93ca-16ca-5e57-835f-036b59f25d63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Compound Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "233361df-2934-52b6-8409-87787fbc9ac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389736} {:answer/id #uuid "0bfa55d8-486d-51be-a4f2-c7daf80570a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "233361df-2934-52b6-8409-87787fbc9ac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389736} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6b17155-b098-59ce-8697-4b721be59f4e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389735} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b46c0c9-5b08-5a0c-9c9e-0dbe02dfb5d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389739} {:answer/id #uuid "401f28b4-450c-5fb5-92f6-b60aac6b8e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b46c0c9-5b08-5a0c-9c9e-0dbe02dfb5d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389739} :answer-field/id #uuid "0296d9ca-6449-57dc-9056-e88a340f66de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389738} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9109cf47-1309-5cc5-920f-0c4a9f90d70b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389742} {:answer/id #uuid "0b8dd9c7-c93a-5e58-94d6-b052dd96294c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9109cf47-1309-5cc5-920f-0c4a9f90d70b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389742} :answer-field/id #uuid "2765f9f5-199f-582b-9383-88bd1a2c2e34" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9797c81c-4349-5761-91d7-aa11ddbab4b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-175917" :question/problem "$$\n{{{1,2}\\cap {3}={1,2,3}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{9\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∧B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is false, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{{1,2}\\cap {3}={1,2,3}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{9\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{false}∧\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93bc0caa-2352-5d02-9ccf-7267dff4be2c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aff03dac-1a8f-5dbf-a4f8-9d2fef0ad08f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∧" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379027} {:answer/id #uuid "4e321d34-1455-5152-bc41-3a72d41cfaa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379028} {:answer/id #uuid "be75db87-a664-505d-b84d-604754c38fda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379029} {:answer/id #uuid "64c60aee-9293-50b9-bd71-a3a552091fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∨" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aff03dac-1a8f-5dbf-a4f8-9d2fef0ad08f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∧" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379027} :ans